<title>ITALY: Finmeccanica H1 loss dips, debt soars.</title>
<headline>Finmeccanica H1 loss dips, debt soars.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30.</p>
<p>    Cons pretax loss		     98.34 vs   118.52</p>
<p>    Cons loss before extraord'ries   70.10 vs    65.65</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		     6,576.63 vs 6,029.42</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	    465.55 vs   601.06</p>
<p>    Operating result		    275.68 vs   243.14</p>
<p>    Net debt			    5,967.79 vs 4,877.93 (end Dec)</p>
<p>    Net assets			  4,984.31 vs 4,879.72</p>
<p>Note: Finmeccanica, Italy's biggest defence and aerospace group, is controlled by state industrial holding company IRI and is due to be privatised next year.  </p>
<p>    Parent pretax profit		  7.2  vs   (68.9)</p>
<p>Finmeccanica said in a statement the first half group pre-tax loss did not yet reflect restructuring at the company.</p>
<p>It added that it expected a significant improvement in its net financial position by the end of the year.</p>
<p>It said in the first half of the year it raised 387 billion lire through disposals and added that at further 613 billion lire of disposals were close to being finalised. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
